# Telegram notification credentials for the social pipeline runners.
# Copy to tools/social/.env (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# Creating the bot (BotFather):
#   1. In Telegram, open @BotFather → /newbot
#   2. Display name: anything (e.g. "Archi Pipeline")
#   3. Username: must end in "bot" (e.g. archi_pipeline_bot)
#   4. Copy the token BotFather returns → TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
#   5. Send any message to your new bot (required once, opens the chat)
#   6. Open https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates and read
#      result[0].message.chat.id → TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telegram channel publisher (publish-telegram-channel.js).
# Posts the daily fact card to a public channel. Reuses TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
# above; TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID stays the private alarm chat and is not touched.
#
#   1. Create the channel in Telegram (public, with a @username, so posts
#      get shareable t.me links)
#   2. Channel → Administrators → Add admin → your bot → enable "Post messages"
#   3. TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_ID is the @username (e.g. @archi_travel_cards);
#      a private channel works too — use its -100… id from getUpdates after
#      forwarding any channel post to the bot
TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bluesky publisher (publish-bluesky.js).
# Use an app password, never the account password:
#   bsky.app → Settings → Privacy and Security → App Passwords → Add App
#   Password (name it e.g. "archi-pipeline"), copy the xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx
#   value once — it is not shown again. Revoking it there kills only this
#   publisher.
# BLUESKY_HANDLE is the full handle, e.g. archi.bsky.social (no @).
BLUESKY_HANDLE=
BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD=
# Only set when self-hosting a PDS; defaults to https://bsky.social.
#BLUESKY_SERVICE=
